      <Placemark>
        <name>Camp 14, Kaechon
South Pyongan Province</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7oSj10XV1UKcUhqB8yX-pb5GO27JVGJm1K9Bpz2ykpsh6-5DIDt9sowTFLDP4-0c4JtM0QUIBKGKYLvPsvhBEWrKpKEqAi6IPooKUqedXuCpdk_ZUFPS4_t_Ri6yq_YmYpIho6pl8Tkkj6V2SFQz6fx33yRQvs-3OyfU1srxf65eJLuRPiiBvN9LzIAVeQWTjF40ly2EFqJqQ?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Kaechon, South Pyongan Province, 39.5717, 126.06215.<br><br>Estimated # of Prisoners: 15,000<br><br>Type of prisoners: Political prisoners<br><br>Type of Labor: Coal mining, logging, farming, raising livestock, and manufacturing<br><br>Detailed analysis of Camp 14, Kaechon can be found in this 2015 HRNK report: https://www.hrnk.org/uploads/pdfs/ASA_HRNK_Camp14_v7_highrezFINAL_11_30_15.pdf]]></description>
