    <Folder>
      <name>Kwan-li-so Believed to be Closed</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Camp 22, Hoeryong
North Hamgyong Province</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR680E_oKI6FN1N_Yi_8H3OV9w933NN5i0ZUgR6K2Rq6VAkIkWgjquGcsjbyj0WI-wjLPQq2CSFpaqAROSNr46ghP6Ik0z2eiEMBUBPYQ998IoYW5LrwQ3gvkzKOpwstQXwuE2nKehDuEURIg1WsiMOrjJOLx7oLbhbPzaRjGBKPa8NEB-nJWU8ppZzsOLJ5g-aW8yZ7T_zqS-Q?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Hoeryong, North Hamgyong Province, 42.54549, 129.91401.<br><br>It is believed that Camp 22, Hoeryong was closed around 2012. The fate and whereabouts of former prisoners at Camp 22, Hoeryong is unknown.<br><br>Estimated # of Prisoners: Up to 50,000<br><br>Type of prisoners: Political prisoners<br><br>Type of Labor: Coal mining, farming, distilling<br><br>Detailed analysis of Camp 22, Hoeryong can be found in this 2013 HRNK report: https://www.hrnk.org/uploads/pdfs/NKHiddenGulag_DavidHawk(2).pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-960-000000</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value>https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR680E_oKI6FN1N_Yi_8H3OV9w933NN5i0ZUgR6K2Rq6VAkIkWgjquGcsjbyj0WI-wjLPQq2CSFpaqAROSNr46ghP6Ik0z2eiEMBUBPYQ998IoYW5LrwQ3gvkzKOpwstQXwuE2nKehDuEURIg1WsiMOrjJOLx7oLbhbPzaRjGBKPa8NEB-nJWU8ppZzsOLJ5g-aW8yZ7T_zqS-Q?fife=s16383</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            129.8776233,42.5844976,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Camp 18, Bukchang
South Pyongan Province</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4i89t14vp9pkwVkvar_hCIYB4bntwi0kRn92Gk0tRJtmlzJhpgBV-aY9nFP_OaBzHFtBm8jq8foBUIWk9Uys-bcXCliaqXnKTukCJ5vfKhyK4VFmgMh1NQrUtHSOCRGvkEihduIC7XJBA8D6jMNblfiNzaHc5iIeA8elGwtzZkpQF8-LgO-JgPa6qHjlXb8p2swzg7p2MpqZg?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Bukchang, South Pyongan Province, 39.55964, 126.08596.<br><br>It is believed that by 2006, nearly all of Camp 18, Bukchang had been decommissioned as a prison camp. Recent analysis shows new activity in the area that may indicate the camp is operational again. <br><br>Estimated # of Prisoners: 27,000<br><br>Type of prisoners: Political prisoners, yeon-jwa-je guilt-by-association prisoners<br><br>Type of Labor: Coal mining, brick making,<br>cement making, glass production, distilling <br><br>Detailed analysis of Camp 18, Bukchang including prisoner testimony can be found in this 2012 HRNK report: https://www.hrnk.org/uploads/pdfs/HRNK_HiddenGulag2_Web_5-18.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-960-000000</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value>https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4i89t14vp9pkwVkvar_hCIYB4bntwi0kRn92Gk0tRJtmlzJhpgBV-aY9nFP_OaBzHFtBm8jq8foBUIWk9Uys-bcXCliaqXnKTukCJ5vfKhyK4VFmgMh1NQrUtHSOCRGvkEihduIC7XJBA8D6jMNblfiNzaHc5iIeA8elGwtzZkpQF8-LgO-JgPa6qHjlXb8p2swzg7p2MpqZg?fife=s16383</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            126.085968,39.5596476,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
    <Folder>
      <name>Unconfirmed Probable Camp Locations</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Kyo-hwa-so No. 8, Yongdam
Kangwon Province</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7I9lwpq830unsuAdVLUzlBsFvboqi5p9Df8nclGcYCuRPGYHI6Rq3Lh07ZLLcCdDew3eopE_gBmC1TyAtW4GtUvcSurc-l3i4TEs_PgoEByrXjCwbkpw1bvcLJ4jbWx-RH3uv_-oDNmOahYkf7Up0jl-OPSBwnEAO7svDCFelJHf_XUlui1hoM_1ntidCwijrs-h6B6XtKn5I?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Yongdam, Kangwon Province, 39° 21’42.91”N 127° 15’53.02”E.<br><br>Estimated # of Prisoners: 2,000<br><br>Type of prisoners: Unknown<br><br>Type of Labor: Unknown <br><br>This location has not been confirmed by HRNK prisoner testimony. Both NKDB and KINU mention Yongdam as an unnumbered kyo-hwa-so located in Chonnae-gun, Kangwon Province. The 2011 NKDB volume, Prisoners in North Korea Today, lists a “Prison No. 8” located in the Seungho area of Pyongang. There is no further information about its current state of operation.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-962-CCCCCC</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value>https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7I9lwpq830unsuAdVLUzlBsFvboqi5p9Df8nclGcYCuRPGYHI6Rq3Lh07ZLLcCdDew3eopE_gBmC1TyAtW4GtUvcSurc-l3i4TEs_PgoEByrXjCwbkpw1bvcLJ4jbWx-RH3uv_-oDNmOahYkf7Up0jl-OPSBwnEAO7svDCFelJHf_XUlui1hoM_1ntidCwijrs-h6B6XtKn5I?fife=s16383</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            127.2649381,39.3613796,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Kyo-hwa-so No. 11, Chung-san
South Pyongan Province</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4YIESuRxRJiWh3YxwgTxqQFTjCD9BlAxtXeP_GM1UA69PHgZ_QdZWrwFTTgpU92iqurhlxhX5fz6SC52W3KjLiby-9IjUVGWx3NoOIv5MkxxFAnwF-7nLMgOvZYnAq0cGFuywqpK0v0TU6swhlkhbU3g8NjvGKm-NVK4CgHL36Dc5rWBPrFARAeSPcLFeUgMrePs4vYn5kSvQ?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Chung-san, South Pyongan Province, 39° 4’40.35”N 125° 26’15.58”E. <br><br>Kyo-hwa-so No. 11, Chung-san is also transliterated as Chonsan, Jungsan, and Jeungsan.<br><br>Estimated # of Prisoners: Over 500<br><br>Type of prisoners: Men, women, border crossers, political prisoners<br><br>Type of Labor: Farming, construction, manufacturing <br><br>Detailed analysis of Kyo-hwa-so No. 11, Chung-san can be found in this 2017 HRNK report: https://www.hrnk.org/uploads/pdfs/Hawk_The_Parallel_Gulag_Web.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-962-CCCCCC</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value>https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4YIESuRxRJiWh3YxwgTxqQFTjCD9BlAxtXeP_GM1UA69PHgZ_QdZWrwFTTgpU92iqurhlxhX5fz6SC52W3KjLiby-9IjUVGWx3NoOIv5MkxxFAnwF-7nLMgOvZYnAq0cGFuywqpK0v0TU6swhlkhbU3g8NjvGKm-NVK4CgHL36Dc5rWBPrFARAeSPcLFeUgMrePs4vYn5kSvQ?fife=s16383</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            125.3218811,39.142294,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Kyo-hwa-so No. 7, Kanggye
Chagang Province</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7_8bYSEQYSGRboxhRFE5hRKvwxlMeA6cRLeJOhSVD7VYArGzeFd-It-gBla34GTaED41v2MlzUTLzcv3vdddztlbFwYSSowD-z8uqX92wU8ZVx1ek6VdGqgJpYXgeO2_lHDFMU4zRDSHIaiOWsovjMhQGoPdRHYAczSMegRRnRq8_fCMkL1QCoEGIJO53Pa0Ij8wJNitKPBgo?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Kanggye City Prison, Kanggye, Changang Province, 40° 57’15.56”N 126° 34’4.31”E. <br><br>Kyo-hwa-so No. 7, Kanggye is also transliterated as Kangkye and Ganggye.<br><br>Estimated # of Prisoners: Unknown<br><br>Type of prisoners: Unknown<br><br>Type of Labor: Unknown <br><br>This location has not been confirmed by HRNK prisoner testimony. It has been listed in NKDB and KINU reports. There is no further information about its current state of operation.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-962-CCCCCC</styleUrl>
