        <name>Kyo-hwa-so No. 9, Hamhung
South Hamgyong Province</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7MrrSU7mNQtNPgUdjKuqHtIxbA2uXL296o6HAvk9jgiaI3qro99-NEnvt9Z_wyvLKRoIdta63Vv2giTKY4aVKIMuDibqUybHx53FGIj_pkLaWrITOwjrzOha8foprzL7kTll0bPqPFDB6qAEbkixDpNMILMIUe2AjXRKBiS7FCmEhxFbG-m2iUG8eZrhmF8bExkvMzP_GgI3c?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Hamhung City Prison, Hamhung, South Hamgyong Province, 39° 57’27.67”N 127° 33’47.40”E. <br><br>Also transliterated as Hamheung, the 2011 NKDB report locates Kyo-hwa-so No. 9, Hamhung Men’s Prison at Hoeyang, Hoesang Area, Hamhung City, while Hamhung Women’s Prison is located at Songwon Village, which is also spelled as Sungwon, Hoesang Area, Hamhung City.<br><br>Estimated # of Prisoners: Over 500<br><br>Type of prisoners: Men, women, political prisoners, forcibly repatriated women<br><br>Type of Labor: Sewing, farming, gold mining <br><br>A second location associated with this camp known as Hamhung Women's Prison is located in Sungwon-ri at 40° 3’29.86”N 127° 40’34.29”E.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6viiQY0P_oEfdJ_qc_kC7AAg4UK5YyMi323ekqubmWwdoaOTA9sPq7WUeQtWpN6X2vGNBn2tQYrYs5qSqGBJnA9ooEpnUZ8PCYyQUfA-WxvCPnLP6G4u8CQoRz4fYRimKV8c6HHIKFxTyCSeECmpX4RTDLP6liS4pGpxsRFvkTI_Ep_ugdmpskk-r4v3VlRQtQlcSZyt4ro5k?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
