        <name>Kyo-hwa-so No. 1, Kaechon
South Pyongan Province</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6Q7hNvgu-WlYI3NI_uRKwVTX1luPTVgv6asLJb8Qp1fowsjSPMjS116hSrbqAk0zmpIuXuFDOv2Hq5MaGrIIFgIzO5e9ieSnsy3VcFASuYak9YoX-yGn8KLHXnJJ8K1eUz7WXoSw2IHfkBA2UkduQ2zOiBm2V8ZpTMOnoswaTZ8fprICkRozpehJqeVzJErUk1txNFU4iJE4Y?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Kaechon, South Pyongan Province, 39° 42’34.72”E, 125° 55’24.78”E.<br><br>Kyo-hwa-so No. 1, Kaechon is also transliterated as Gaechon, which is located in Yaksu-dong, Kaechon City and thought to be one of the oldest kyo-hwa-so prison camps. <br><br>Estimated # of Prisoners: 4,000 to 6,000 <br><br>Type of prisoners: Men, women, political prisoners, border crossers, genuine criminal offenders, Japanese-Koreans<br><br>Type of Labor: Textile production, Leather manufacturing<br><br>Detailed analysis of Kyo-hwa-so No. 1, Kaechon can be found in this 2020 HRNK report: https://www.hrnk.org/uploads/pdfs/Bermudez_Kaechon_FINAL.pdf<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR5vdATbKvQ8S2ZvSB5gNapQzTndAib_e6BWHiZawruOwMwx__zbXtlgHCwKthMUuN7azxkAiAw4nMzEcxSu8gcAuwl8hjbpW3OD_tm9OwxnOTiwfkNe0OvRdF266UXCrP0DQVQirnv35lEdcD1HN5FQhJQ8WX03onZBbqoqCQmvTP3AuPeqSW5VCbOn6pnxf3-Dt7T1kA5oW9U?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-959-F8971B</styleUrl>
