      <Placemark>
        <name>Kyo-hwa-so No. 4, Kangdong
Pyongyang City</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6uyAEutgb01S_cPtetf7baUqd7PKKDQXyhMTi8CB_VKx5i4ONoB6oW2r0mJGLuANh5DxD_fbI1WnlUxcamyiltuu0fEUeonqpirqJZv0tUIPl7V-WfmNBjdMDKAQfT6e7hPEDIkiaHW5FJum8xWB3vrSRQQXRprxA6QVMQltNBsZpNdVWf5s1jqwJJkYuFttpA6oMJUZWdKQA?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Samdung-ri, Kangdong-kun, South Pyongan Province,  39° 0’31.24”N 126° 9’12.42”E.<br><br>Also transliterated as Gangdong, Kyo-hwa-so No. 4, Kangdong is located in Chael-kol on the eastern outskirts of Pyongyang close to South Pyongan Province. <br><br>Estimated # of Prisoners: 1,000 to 4,000<br><br>Type of prisoners: Men, civilian and military offenders, political prisoners<br><br>Type of Labor: Limestone and cement production<br><br>Detailed analysis of Kyo-hwa-so No. 4, Kangdong can be found in this 2019 HRNK report: https://www.hrnk.org/uploads/pdfs/Bermudez_Kangdong_FINALFINAL.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-959-F8971B</styleUrl>
