      <Placemark>
        <name>Kyo-hwa-so No. 12, Jongo-ri
North Hamgyong Province</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6ss6rypwdexr0l_4blIpGX7RPcG-lCKgsHgsU5d9EoTovTV0T6vMpKoJM_pDC33ikVF4l84w6mdXobtdEhsrU28nryNhWL_d2FlhRfBG2Xl8JTI8LnY1uo2Oq8OGGNhRAJ9w_s26spEPg7UNGvJT2YjrToVA-h99ir5dZQmuzCHx4P_MGTcapF3ULdBTPlY-RWfEerh-upamw?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Jongo-ri, North Hamgyong Province, 42° 12’34.00”N 129° 45’18.14”E.<br><br>Kyo-hwa-so No. 12, Jongo-ri is also transliterated as Chongo-ri.<br><br>Estimated # of Prisoners: 2,300 to 2,500<br><br>Type of prisoners: Men, women, border crossers, political prisoners, forcibly repatriated women<br><br>Type of Labor: Copper and iron mining, farming, brick making, wig and eyelash production<br><br>Detailed analysis of Kyo-hwa-so No. 12, Jongo-ri can be found in this 2016 HRNK report: https://www.hrnk.org/uploads/pdfs/ASA_HRNK_Camp12_201608_v10_LR.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-959-F8971B</styleUrl>
