    <Folder>
      <name>Kyo-hwa-so Believed to be Closed</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Kyo-hwa-so No. 22, Oro
South Hamgyong Province</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7F6ae9x3EEz_FySJfNLm3pSzTQrqMdIPpyNv4DuAAaeTeL7OkIwc80JLs2oc3IGY5AO2nY-Xgp29W6egmrkwGGYBUfCi5D0DWXjjwPRIPV5Ay3gJ1qRYbJzcj7JjYDS03DHIA9PRdcvRxsoH9zdx3QSlWCOnE83jgDGnlOW2Ox6F7JyqQ5Q76zJPbVwQOtH661-uDd2JpcB2Q?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Tongjung-ri, Oro, South Hamgyong Province, 40° 2’35.88”N 127° 31’24.94”E.<br><br>It is believed that Kyo-hwa-so No. 22, Oro was closed around 2008. <br><br>Estimated # of Prisoners: 1,100<br><br>Type of prisoners: Men, women, political prisoners, short term prisoners<br><br>Type of Labor:  Construction<br><br>This location is not yet confirmed. It has been listed in NKDB and KINU reports as well as identified in prisoner testimony. There is no further information about its current state of operation.<br><br>A second location associated with this camp is located in Pungho-ri at 40° 1’19.71”N 127° 25’55.91”E.<br><br>A third location associated with this camp is located in Sangtong-ri at 40° 5’35.68”N 127° 21’26.45”E.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4HLYZqVgHVXsaE8A-U-yPEzKG3KXaWLWT4hrdYHkBkbq6YDDuiS8pyqVLlYZEQ0CLkXAIWQ_W7f6GxerBWISWHXG_rfYD2juQjNlhGpBJ9p4msMPmVtzYotc6kQFYVCSgxjTtHwhd8wS97GG3UGonr7R67b8VNZ-k7MMzzmSLtLpv7mA1rUgMzfqc9eV1uDUxFfcQgrO_IdUo?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7W5adwOKDFgjrT3q6iVZk6OmQ75RjF9fTo3XMAnV1-j3ahK2WEsaqcsJfRwifVHo_hSpulQknPEAtwKO37C8zIGCMOBOIeDVqeb1h3n3fh_a9Yn6FMrCwRxKw_g8JsWFf-5muj-H55SBn377QiFgbWwQOP6xOJ-AK62Xf1t-adegxooXxkIIm3cHs2a8AJPgeP-WpTa-1SO7c?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
