      <Placemark>
        <name>Kyo-hwa-so No. 77, Danchon
South Hamgyong Province</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR68h41Q2jCwn2jBd5_qSGGBK-U7_XTV6IoG5PnR-zIpXj27GnTABaQJSMGjMlgWwwQLE5boyAANr-LVs50WO2etx8_hZ_aSuSi_e0CvthFbGkCvQy-1EPCVQvbZV6G2iKNFzna2b3LzgCxTAfrQAWw49dU-LgFGWPYEwFSDkV8JFS1OdQcZOfj0xmNZpiaDddqDfC7OAQbgFTQ?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Hangguil-dong, Danchon, South Hamgyong Province, 40° 26’15.36”N 128° 53’57.06”E.<br><br>It is believed that Kyo-hwa-so No. 77, Danchon was closed around 1997. However, the locations identified here appear to be in operation.<br><br>Estimated # of Prisoners: Uknown<br><br>Type of prisoners: Men, political prisoners, genuine criminal offenders, border crossers<br><br>Type of Labor: Gold mining<br><br>This location is not yet confirmed. It has been listed in NKDB reports as well as identified in prisoner testimony. There is no further information about its current state of operation.<br><br>A second location associated with this camp is located in Sangjang at 40° 24’57.26”N 128° 53’46.11”E.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR5M4T-ldr-YKDEeAqGIJe9CnDsBdKdYh6bffbLG-bi2s0dPqerGpQRAtqqZ17f1V7bjWmlLGR7grnr3OiQS2JD2aEU0fLni1EOGvQSN7vuhNh6dhzonQgDYzLpdd8zNQzfhUToUOQ9ZWRZHeXRbg9wKI10wUiJ2OkRzjyV-l5zPFrFjDmOXMC87m4TeQz7WPKgaPlbkKy1kVWE?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
